# Bifrost Forge World Project Context

Bifrost Forge World is a ReactJS / Electron application for modelling, deploying, and debugging BPMN 2.0 process models. It is designed around extensibility: core functionality is delivered through internal modules — the same mechanism available to third-party developers.

## Folder Structure

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `studio-sdk/` | Public SDK: types, contracts, and reusable React components for plugins |
| `studio/src/bifrost/` | Core framework: entrypoints, mediators, contracts, services |
| `studio/src/modules/` | Built-in modules (std, bpmn-editor, engine-*, etc.) |
| `studio/src/components/` | Shared internal React components |

## Core Architecture

- **Commands** — All interactions flow through `bifrost.commands.executeCommand()`. Modules MUST NOT call each other directly.
- **Modules** — Register document types, menus, icons, panes, and commands via the Bifrost API. Foundation modules (`engine-core`, `bpmn-core`) communicate with consumers via events on shared mediators, never by accessing consumer code directly.
- **Editor Documents** — Each document type binds a URI pattern to a model, renderer, and inspector.
- **Module Discovery** — Extensions register diagram-js modules via `bpmn.modeler.registerModule` for BPMN modeler customization.

